[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:It Could be Worse]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.39]Had the writer's money been stolen? | 作者的钱被偷了吗？
[00:15.33]I entered the hotel manager's office and sat down. | 我走进饭店经理的办公室，坐了下来。
[00:20.13]I had just lost ￡50 and I felt very upset. | 我刚刚丢了50英镑，感到非常烦恼。
[00:26.39]'I left the money in my room,' I said, 'and it's not there now.  ' | “我把钱放在房间里了，”我说，“可现在没有了。”
[00:33.33]The manager was sympathetic, but he could do nothing. | 经理深表同情，但无能为力。
[00:38.93]'Everyone's losing money these days,' he said. | “现在大家都在丢钱，”他说。
[00:44.08]He started to complain about this wicked world but was interrupted by a knock at the door. | 他开始抱怨起这个邪恶的世道来，却被一阵敲门声打断了。
[00:52.53]A girl came in and put an envelope on his desk. | 一个姑娘走了进来，把一个信封放在了他的桌上。
[00:56.98]It contained ￡50. | 里面装着50英镑。
[00:59.97]'I found this outside this gentleman's room,' she said. | “我在这位先生的房门外捡到的，”她说。
[01:05.16]'Well,' I said to the manager,'there is still some honesty in this world!' | “好了，”我对经理说，“这个世界上还是有诚实可言的！”
